      instructorVoice:
        "Former Adventists who were once deeply embedded in the church often have extensive knowledge of Ellen White's writings — and they use this knowledge selectively. They will quote her most extreme statements out of context, her most culturally conditioned counsels as if they were timeless absolutes, and her most human moments as if they disprove her prophetic gift. This selective quoting is extraordinarily effective because most current Adventists do not know Ellen White's writings well enough to identify the misrepresentation.\n\nConsider how the devil himself used selective Scripture quotation: 'If thou be the Son of God, cast thyself down: for it is written, He shall give his angels charge concerning thee' (Matthew 4:6). Satan quoted Psalm 91 accurately — but applied it deceptively. In the same way, a former SDA may quote Ellen White accurately while applying her words deceptively. The words are real; the context is missing; the conclusion is false.\n\n'For we are not as many, which corrupt the word of God: but as of sincerity, but as of God, in the sight of God speak we in Christ' (2 Corinthians 2:17). Your defense must not corrupt Ellen White in the opposite direction — presenting only her best statements. Honesty requires you to understand both the difficult and the beautiful in her writings.",
