      instructorVoice:
        "In the age of social media, the former SDA does not depart alone. They join Facebook groups, Reddit communities, YouTube channels, and podcasts specifically designed for ex-Adventists. These communities serve a legitimate need — people who have left need a place to process their experiences. But they also function as echo chambers that reinforce departure narratives, amplify grievances, and create a collective identity built on shared rejection of Adventism.\n\nThe psychological dynamics of these communities are powerful. Confirmation bias ensures that members see only the evidence that supports their decision to leave. Social reinforcement rewards the most dramatic departure stories and the most devastating critiques. Groupthink discourages any member from expressing doubt about their decision to leave. The result is a self-reinforcing cycle that makes return almost psychologically impossible — not because the evidence demands it, but because the social cost of admitting doubt is too high.\n\n'For the time will come when they will not endure sound doctrine; but after their own lusts shall they heap to themselves teachers, having itching ears; And they shall turn away their ears from the truth, and shall be turned unto fables' (2 Timothy 4:3-4). The echo chamber is not a search for truth — it is a search for validation. And validation feels exactly like truth, which is what makes it so dangerous.",
